{
  "_comment": [
    "Magic-byte vectors shared by the Go sniffer (transport/normalize/locator)",
    "and the TypeScript one (packages/ui-shared/src/lib/sniffMime.ts).",
    "",
    "They cannot share code across the language boundary, so they share this",
    "table instead, and both sides assert against it. Two sniffers in one",
    "program is only safe if they cannot disagree: before this file they did,",
    "and an iPhone photo submitted as a video input reference was served",
    "inline as video/mp4 and downloaded as .mp4 by the server while the Agent",
    "Dashboard called the same bytes image/heic.",
    "",
    "prefix is hex. Bytes past the signature do not matter to either sniffer,",
    "so a vector is only as long as the signature it exercises."
  ],
